{"id": "EUVD-2026-86831", "enisaUuid": "1934c600-2bf9-3dc3-b426-f0130b23c66c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmptcp: close race between scheduler and state change\n\nThe mptcp scheduler may race with subflow sockets state change: data\ntransmission on the selected socket may fail and a later release could\ntry to use mss_now reset to 0 for a divide operation.\n\nAddress the issue by explicitly checking for the critical scenario.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:08:41", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d74b2e26b54a7dae1d87c1f19ae0d6db500e5e03", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5883ae880f51edc4b1484e787473b865b6159ead", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a926b5df8efdfbac07e2fb7fafb21849a2ad9c0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f11430d51ff8365bc51b670bc3002b65ae4c6b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a09c87abf10a0a7e203137c75b5381aa63d9b31d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4c856f3c151a2f3fa237caa651c44015916ca584", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42064de57fb83231fcc89663a94885f228a1ee53"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7c5c-gph2-xxg8", "CVE-2026-97523"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.67, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0963d780-1169-3952-8ffd-761abd78a76e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "14ee00ad-d7a5-34d4-ae08-dc5505a43446", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1a3d2ee4-0da1-304c-938e-91b9e1e25d66", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "26beb3ea-0131-38ed-8358-b970c2350223", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c886d70286bf3ad411eb3d689328a67f7102c6ae <8f11430d51ff8365bc51b670bc3002b65ae4c6b7"}, {"id": "28014bad-d2a4-3794-bd08-6c0154f4